---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Tracepod"
  description="What data the Tracepod website collects, why, and what happens to it."
>

  <section class="privacy-section section">
    <div class="container privacy-inner">
      <div class="eyebrow">Privacy</div>
      <h1 class="heading-lg">Short, because there isn&rsquo;t much to tell.</h1>
      <p class="body-md privacy-updated">Last updated: 13 July 2026</p>

      <div class="privacy-body">
        <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
        <p>
          Tracepod is an independent software project, not a registered company. This
          website is operated by the project&rsquo;s maintainer. If you have any question
          about this policy, use the <a href="/contact">contact form</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          The only personal data this site collects is what you type into the contact
          form: your name, email address, an optional company name, and your message.
          We use it for exactly one thing &mdash; replying to you. We don&rsquo;t add you to a
          mailing list, and we don&rsquo;t send marketing.
        </p>

        <h2>How the contact form works</h2>
        <p>
          Form submissions are delivered by
          <a href="https://web3forms.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Web3Forms</a>,
          which forwards your message to our inbox and states that it does not store
          submission contents after delivery. From then on your message lives in our
          email, retained only as long as the correspondence is useful. Want it deleted?
          Ask, and it&rsquo;s gone.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p>
          There are no analytics, no ad trackers, and no cookies. The site stores a
          single value in your browser&rsquo;s local storage &mdash; your light/dark theme
          preference &mdash; and it never leaves your machine.
        </p>

        <h2>Hosting</h2>
        <p>
          The site is served by GitHub Pages. Like any web host, GitHub may log visitor
          IP addresses for security purposes; see the
          <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
          We have no access to, and keep no copy of, those logs.
        </p>

        <h2>The software is a different story &mdash; deliberately</h2>
        <p>
          The Tracepod sensor and CLI run entirely inside your infrastructure and phone
          home to nobody. Profiles, images, and SBOMs stay in your cluster and your
          registry. There is no telemetry in the open-source tooling.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
.privacy-section { padding-top: var(--space-16); }
.privacy-inner { max-width: 720px; }
.privacy-updated { margin-top: var(--space-3); color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.875rem; }

.privacy-body { margin-top: var(--space-8); }
.privacy-body h2 {
  font-size: 1.1rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--text-primary);
  margin-top: var(--space-8);
  margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
}
.privacy-body p {
  color: var(--text-secondary);
  line-height: 1.7;
  font-size: 0.95rem;
}
.privacy-body a { color: var(--accent); }
</style>
